license: MIT
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23442766"
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23442766"
repository-code: "https://github.com/pablobernabeu/secure_local_HPC_speech_transcription"
abstract: "A local transcription workflow built on OpenAI's Whisper models, for research recordings that cannot be sent to a cloud service. It keeps custody of the audio, runs on a laptop or a Slurm cluster, and adds speaker diarisation, name masking and a measured layer of defensive post-processing. Keeping custody is not de-identification: the masking and voice-anonymisation features are documented as bounded, with the measurements behind that in the accompanying paper."
keywords:
  - speech transcription
  - speaker diarisation
  - whisper
  - local
  - high-performance computing
  - HPC
  - data privacy
  - data protection
  - GDPR
